":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.11258562735883916,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.111977688377718,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.49763,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Exodus Movement, Inc. operates as a financial technology for blockchain and digital asset industry in the United States. The company develops Exodus Platform, an un-hosted self-custodial digital asset wallet that provides access to the world of decentralized finance and the power of blockchain. It also offers fiat on and off-ramps to facilitate an exchange for users to buy digital assets with fiat currency through bank transfer, credit or debit card, and Apple Pay; and staking services, which allows users to stake digital assets in their Exodus wallets. The company offers its products directly through the Exodus Platform, including storing, sending, and receiving digital assets through the wallet functionality. Exodus Movement, Inc. was founded in 2015 and is based in Omaha, Nebraska.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jon Paul Richardson | Chairperson & CEO | Age 41 | Compensation: $638,416 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 215 people. Revenue per employee of $565K ranks in the above the sector median among Technology peers. Stock-based compensation of $63K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["Exodus Movement, Inc. is a micro-cap technology business with a $134M market cap on $122M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +5% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 23% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 14-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The company is burning through $26M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -35.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 11.3% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and stock-based comp at 11% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 50% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 23% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Technology peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (38% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 124% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Exodus (EXOD) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"fool.com","link":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/11/10/exodus-exod-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/?source=iedfolrf0000001","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794321629.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.402,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Exodus outlines plan to cut annual costs by approximately $30M going into 2027 as payments mix grows (NYSE:EXOD)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4669496-exodus-outlines-plan-to-cut-annual-costs-by-approximately-30m-going-into-2027-as-payments-mix","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794289389.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.649,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Exodus Movement, Inc. (EXOD) Reports Q3 Loss, Beats Revenue Estimates","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3026862/exodus-movement-inc-exod-reports-q3-loss-beats-revenue-estimates?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_4-3026862","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794272702.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.318,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"(EXOD) and the Role of Price-Sensitive Allocations","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/11/EXOD_and_the_Role_of_Price-Sensitive_Allocations_102826105001_1793199001.html","date":"2026-10-28","timestamp":179319